Z||000004||AkursedX||06-09-2001||04:54 PM||||I would recommend staying away from Castrol Syntec oil though.  I would keep going with synthectic oils, but change the brand (Mobil 1, Penzoil, Valvoline)  But I have heard plenty bad things about Castrol Syntec.  It seems that they derive part of it from Crude oil or something of the sort and apparently it's not that good of an oil.  <BR>I believe i heard this info on this forum before, so maybe someone can back me up on this.||||reg||4
Z||000005||rogergarrison||06-09-2001||07:19 PM||||this has all been beat to death guys. All I know is personal experience, but Ive used Castrol full Synthetic since i put my engine in, (well after first break in oil) Ive driven it hard for 86,0000 miles now with absolutely no engine probs. I cant make it use a drop of oil between changes, my OP stays up around 70 psi all the time, even after long stretches of 100+ mph.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
